MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I'm not sure what the type of egcVect and the other arguments are, but it's likely that whatever value return by egcVect.toString() is not valid R syntax.

Instead of trying to mash together an R script (which looks to be in excess of 254k), you should use the Script API for passing R objects directly to the engine:

engine.put("x", 4);
engine.put("y", new double[] { 1d, 2d, 3d, 4d });
engine.put("z", new DoubleArrayVector(1,2,3,4,5));
engine.eval("x + y + z");

See Pushing data from Java to R <http://docs.renjin.org/en/latest/moving-data-between-java-and-r-code.html#pushing-data-from-java-to-r> on docs.renjin.org <http://docs.renjin.org> for more examples.

Alex

